# Local GitHub Actions runner (nektos/act) — used by `task act`.
#
# The platform map is the one decision that matters: act's default image
# (node:16-buster-slim) cannot run this repository's jobs, which need apt,
# git with full history, and a glibc Python. catthehacker's image is the
# community-standard Ubuntu-like runner image for act and preinstalls most
# of what jobs assume; the rest (uv, task, toolchains) the jobs install
# themselves, exactly as they do on GitHub's runners.
-P ubuntu-24.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-24.04

# Reuse pulled images instead of re-pulling on every run; a fresh pull of the
# runner image costs more than most jobs here.
--pull=false

# Keep job logs readable when a job fails mid-step.
--verbose
